// Seller Home — Knowledge page data
// =====================================================================
// Consumed by src/views/knowledge.html (which composes _home_left_nav
// via the .seller-home shell). gulpfile.js's getData() auto-merges
// this file into the template's local scope by filename → template lookup.
//
// This file intentionally carries ONLY page-specific bindings. Global
// nav content (navPrimary, navFooter, recents) is pulled at template
// time from home.json via the `readData("home").<key>` Nunjucks
// global registered in gulpfile.js — the Knowledge page is a sub-
// surface of the Seller Home nav, so both pages must show the same
// primary items and recents list without duplication.
//
// Fields:
//   • pageTitle          (string) window title + <main aria-label>
//   • navActive          (string) id of the currently-active left-nav
//                        item. The renderNavItem macro in
//                        _home_left_nav.html applies `.is-active` +
//                        `aria-current="page"` when this equals
//                        item.id. "knowledge" matches the renamed
//                        entry in home.json → navPrimary.
//   • newKnowledgeLabel  (string) label for the header CTA button.
//                        Kept as data so future localization + a
//                        possible label change ("Add document",
//                        "New file") happens without a template edit.
//   • header             (object) misc header content:
//                        - heading   (string) H1 displayed above the
//                                    document list; matches the SLDS
//                                    Titles/font-scale-3 treatment
//                                    from the Figma frame 8931:383002.
//   • banner             (object) copy for the promo banner at the top
//                        of the scrollable body, above the search field —
//                        badge, title, description, run-summary stats,
//                        and CTA label, laid out beside the
//                        illustration. Omit the whole
//                        object and the template renders nothing — no
//                        empty box, no reserved space — so turning the
//                        banner off is a data-only edit. Fields:
//                          - badge        (string) small pill above the
//                                         title. Short: it's a label, not
//                                         a sentence, and it does not
//                                         wrap.
//                          - title        (string) banner headline.
//                                         Rendered as a `<p>`, NOT a
//                                         heading — the page already has
//                                         exactly one H1 ("Knowledge"),
//                                         and a promo headline shouldn't
//                                         compete with it in the document
//                                         outline or a screen reader's
//                                         heading list.
//                          - description  (string) supporting paragraph.
//                          - stats        (array of strings, optional)
//                                         run-summary facts shown on one
//                                         line under the description,
//                                         joined by "∙" separators the
//                                         TEMPLATE emits (each is
//                                         `aria-hidden`, so a screen
//                                         reader reads the facts as a
//                                         list instead of "bullet
//                                         operator" three times). Store
//                                         the phrases only — no
//                                         separators, no trailing
//                                         punctuation. Any length: the
//                                         line wraps item-by-item at
//                                         narrow widths rather than
//                                         breaking mid-phrase. Omit or
//                                         empty the array and the line
//                                         disappears.
//                          - buttonLabel  (string) CTA label. The button
//                                         is a stub — it carries a
//                                         `data-sh-knowledge-setup` hook
//                                         for a later phase to bind, and
//                                         does nothing when clicked
//                                         today.
//
//                        The illustration itself is NOT configured here.
//                        It's a CSS `background-image` on
//                        `.knowledge-banner__illustration` in home.scss,
//                        because the authored markup for that element is
//                        an empty div — which is also what lets the art
//                        fill and crop to whatever height this copy
//                        happens to need. Swapping the art is a one-line
//                        change in home.scss, not a data edit.
//   • search             (object) copy for the doc-list search field
//                        (Figma frame 8931:383736 → "Input - Search").
//                        Filtering is client-only (see home.js →
//                        bindKnowledgeSearch): trimmed, case-
//                        insensitive substring match against each
//                        row's `name` + `type`. Fields:
//                          - label         (string) accessible label
//                                          for the input (rendered as
//                                          `slds-assistive-text` for a
//                                          visually iconic input that
//                                          still names itself to a
//                                          screen reader).
//                          - placeholder   (string) input placeholder.
//                          - clearLabel    (string) accessible label
//                                          + tooltip for the clear (×)
//                                          button that surfaces when
//                                          the field has a value.
//   • emptyState         (object) copy for the "no matches" state
//                        shown in the doc-list slot when a search
//                        query filters out every row. Kept as data so
//                        the same partial can be reused for a future
//                        "no documents yet" first-run state with
//                        different copy. Fields:
//                          - title         (string) primary heading
//                                          for the empty state.
//                          - description   (string) supporting text
//                                          below the heading.
//   • documents          (array) doc-list rows rendered by
//                        _home_knowledge_list.html → renderKnowledgeDocRow.
//                        Each item is a stable-shaped record so a
//                        future API can drop in without template edits.
//                        Fields:
//                          - id         (string, required) URL-safe,
//                                       collision-free identifier used
//                                       as the DOM hook (`data-sh-
//                                       knowledge-doc-id`), the menu's
//                                       id-suffix, and the STABLE
//                                       routing key for the doc detail
//                                       view. Keep kebab-case.
//
//                                       Stable-route contract: the
//                                       drill-in view is a single
//                                       template (knowledge_document_
//                                       detail.html) reached at
//                                       /knowledge_document_detail.html
//                                       ?id=<id>. Every id here is a
//                                       durable, shareable URL — safe
//                                       to bookmark, copy-paste into a
//                                       DM, or link to from an external
//                                       system. The extensionless
//                                       shortcut /knowledge_document_
//                                       detail?id=<id> resolves to the
//                                       same page via server.js's
//                                       `extensions: ['html']` config.
//                                       DO NOT rename an id after it
//                                       ships — bookmarks would 404.
//                                       Renames land in `documentAliases`
//                                       below (legacy → current
//                                       forwarding); the resolver in
//                                       knowledge_document_detail.js
//                                       consults it when a direct id
//                                       lookup misses.
//                          - name       (string, required) primary text
//                                       shown on the row. Long names
//                                       ellipsize via CSS; the full
//                                       string is exposed through the
//                                       row's native `title` tooltip.
//                          - badge      (string, optional) short pill
//                                       label, right-aligned in the row
//                                       just left of the overflow menu,
//                                       in the same purple as the page
//                                       banner's badge. Currently set on
//                                       ONE row ("New Learnings" on the
//                                       most recently updated doc) so it
//                                       reads as a callout; the sibling
//                                       docs keep the field commented
//                                       out rather than deleted, so
//                                       badging the whole set again is
//                                       an uncomment. Keep it to one or
//                                       two words: the badge never
//                                       shrinks, so a long label eats
//                                       the name's truncation budget.
//                                       Omit and the row renders
//                                       name-only.
//
//                                       NOT part of the search index —
//                                       `bindKnowledgeSearch` matches
//                                       `name` + `type` only, so a
//                                       badge label is not a findable
//                                       term.
//                          - type       (string, required) high-level
//                                       taxonomy label displayed in the
//                                       row's secondary metadata line
//                                       (e.g. "Document"). Kept as data
//                                       so a future doc kind ("Skill
//                                       File", "Playbook") reads through
//                                       without template edits.
//                          - fileType   (string, required) sprite id in
//                                       /assets/icons/doctype-sprite/svg/
//                                       symbols.svg → picks the yellow
//                                       doctype icon (txt / pdf / …).
//                                       Must be one of the sprites SLDS
//                                       ships; unknown values render a
//                                       blank <use> and swallow the
//                                       icon visually. Ignored when
//                                       `iconSrc` is set, but keep it
//                                       populated anyway — see below.
//                          - iconSrc    (string, optional) path under
//                                       /assets to a bitmap icon that
//                                       REPLACES the `fileType` sprite
//                                       glyph on this row. For doc kinds
//                                       SLDS ships no glyph for; the
//                                       Auto-Learning documents use it
//                                       to render the purple "AI" file
//                                       icon instead of a generic TXT
//                                       page. Painted into the same
//                                       24-px box as the sprite, so
//                                       rows stay aligned whichever
//                                       branch renders.
//
//                                       Source art should be square and
//                                       at least 48×48 so it survives
//                                       retina; the AI icon is 96×96.
//                                       Non-square art letterboxes
//                                       rather than stretching.
//
//                                       Set BOTH this and `fileType`:
//                                       deleting `iconSrc` then falls
//                                       straight back to the sprite
//                                       instead of rendering an empty
//                                       icon box.
//                          - updatedAt  (string, required) preformatted
//                                       "MMMM D" date shown after the
//                                       type on the metadata line, where
//                                       the row template prefixes the
//                                       word "Updated" → "Document ·
//                                       Updated July 28". Store the date
//                                       ONLY (no "Updated", no year);
//                                       the year is dropped because
//                                       every doc is current-year and
//                                       the row reads tighter without
//                                       it. Preformatted here (not a raw
//                                       date) so the render path stays
//                                       locale-agnostic; a future i18n
//                                       phase can move this into a
//                                       date-string producer.
//
//                                       Also feeds the detail page's
//                                       "Last edited by <updatedBy> ·
//                                       <updatedAt>" caption, so a
//                                       format change here shows up in
//                                       two places.
//                          - updatedBy  (string, optional) display name
//                                       of the last editor. Rendered on
//                                       the document-detail page as
//                                       "Last edited by <updatedBy> ·
//                                       <updatedAt>". Omitted from the
//                                       list row itself so the compact
//                                       row shape stays unchanged.
//                          - markdown   (string, required for the
//                                       detail page) full document body
//                                       in the same subset the shared
//                                       `KnowledgeDocumentView` module
//                                       parses (headings `#`/`##`/`###`,
//                                       paragraphs, `-` ul, `1.` ol,
//                                       inline `**bold**`, `*italic*`,
//                                       `` `code` ``, `[link](url)`).
//                                       The detail page reads this
//                                       field client-side by matching
//                                       the row's id against
//                                       `?id=<id>` on the URL.
//                          - href       (string, optional) target URL
//                                       for the row's anchor. Omit or
//                                       leave empty and the row
//                                       template defaults to
//                                       `/knowledge_document_detail.html
//                                       ?id=<id>`, which is the built-in
//                                       Seller Home detail page. Set an
//                                       explicit `href` only when a
//                                       specific doc should route
//                                       somewhere else (a legacy URL,
//                                       an external link, etc.).
//   • documentActions    (array) menu items shown in every doc row's
//                        overflow menu (⋮). Rendered by the row macro
//                        in the same order they appear here, so
//                        reordering is a data-only edit. Fields:
//                          - id     (string, required) action slug
//                                   emitted in `sh:knowledge-doc-
//                                   action` details (`{action, docId}`).
//                                   Kebab-case, stable across releases.
//                          - label  (string, required) visible menu-
//                                   item text.
//                          - icon   (string, optional) utility-sprite id
//                                   for the item's leading glyph. Same
//                                   pattern the review-row overflow uses.
//
// Phase 4 landed: search input (Figma 8931:383736) filters the doc
// list client-side against `documents[*].name` + `documents[*].type`
// and swaps the list for an `emptyState`-driven "no matches" view
// when nothing survives the query. Row-level overflow menu, doc
// list, and mock-data-driven rendering are also in from Phase 3.
//
// Phase 5 landed: each document now carries a full markdown body +
// author. Rows link to `/knowledge_document_detail.html?id=<id>` by
// default (template-side fallback in `_home_knowledge_list.html`);
// the detail page reads the SAME `documents[]` catalog via Nunjucks
// `readData("knowledge")` so there's exactly one source of truth for
// document data — no duplicated JSON, no drift between list + detail.
{
  "pageTitle": "Knowledge",
  "navActive": "knowledge",
  "newKnowledgeLabel": "New Knowledge",
  "header": {
    "heading": "Knowledge"
  },
  "banner": {
    "badge": "New",
    "title": "Get deals done faster with<br>auto-learning",
    "description": "With agents that learn automatically, you get the highest-quality prospects, personalized emails, and AI-powered workflows based on your sales process and customer needs.",
    "stats": [
      { "label": "Ran for", "value": "2 days and 18 hours" },
      { "label": "Read", "value": "1.4k calls and 10.8k emails" }
    ],
    "buttonLabel": "Got it"
  },
  "search": {
    "label": "Search knowledge",
    "placeholder": "Search...",
    "clearLabel": "Clear search"
  },
  "emptyState": {
    "title": "No knowledge found",
    "description": "Try a different search term."
  },

  // Tabs that filter the document list (see knowledge.html + home.js →
  // bindKnowledgeTabs). Each document's `tab` field decides which tab it
  // appears under; a document with no `tab` falls under "learnings".
  // `defaultTabId` is the tab shown on first paint.
  "tabs": {
    "defaultTabId": "learnings",
    "items": [
      { "id": "learnings", "label": "Learnings" },
      { "id": "sources",   "label": "Sources" }
    ]
  },

  "documentActions": [
    { "id": "download", "label": "Download", "icon": "download" },
    { "id": "delete",   "label": "Delete",   "icon": "delete"   }
  ],

  // KnowledgeGenerationMetadata — shared generation metadata for the
  // Auto-Learning run that produced the auto-learned documents (the
  // ones carrying `badge: "Auto-learned"` in `documents[]` below).
  //
  // Lineage. In the pre-split doc this lived at the bottom of the body
  // as `## Footer: Parameter Snapshot for Deterministic Re-Run`,
  // rendered as an unordered list. The split refactor lifts that list
  // out of every doc's markdown into ONE shared record so the five
  // sibling docs don't each carry a copy that has to be kept in sync.
  //
  // Field mapping (Parameter Snapshot bullet → camelCased field):
  //   run_id                → runId
  //   plan_version          → planVersion
  //   lookback_days         → lookbackDays
  //   opp_cap               → opportunityCap
  //   transcripts_per_opp   → transcriptsPerOpportunity
  //   min_theme_support     → minimumThemeSupport
  //   source                → source
  //   opportunities_analyzed→ opportunitiesAnalyzed
  //   transcripts_read      → transcriptsRead
  //   skill_key             → skillKey
  //
  // Reference. Each of the five split docs joins to this record via its
  // `generationMetadataId` field (all five point at
  // "auto-learning-run-2026-07-28"). One-to-many by design — a future
  // second Auto-Learning run would add a second record here and stamp
  // its own id onto the docs it produced.
  //
  // Consumers. Not inlined into the detail-page config today (see
  // `knowledge_document_detail.html`'s `<script id="sh-knowledge-doc-
  // detail-config">` block — only `catalog` and the chrome strings are
  // projected). The intentional omission keeps the reader surface
  // quiet; wiring this into a "Run parameters" panel is a data-only
  // template change when we're ready (add `generationMetadata` to the
  // JSON blob, then look up `doc.generationMetadataId` client-side).
  "generationMetadata": {
    "id": "auto-learning-run-2026-07-28",
    "runId": "9e2b819a-5f71-413f-b95b-4362df9ee1e1",
    "planVersion": 1,
    "lookbackDays": 90,
    "opportunityCap": 10,
    "transcriptsPerOpportunity": 4,
    "minimumThemeSupport": 3,
    "source": "Salesforce VoiceCall → ConversationEntry (via ConversationId)",
    "opportunitiesAnalyzed": "9 of 10 cap; Tipalti excluded due to no-show",
    "transcriptsRead": "23 of 24 fetched; one no-show excluded",
    "skillKey": "customer_discovery_skill_v1"
  },

  // ExecutionLogEntry[] — chronological run log for the same
  // Auto-Learning run described by `generationMetadata` above.
  //
  // Lineage. In the pre-split doc this lived in the body as
  // `## Execution Log`, rendered as a numbered list of `**Task N:**`
  // lines followed by a bold "Skipped actions:" subsection. The split
  // refactor lifts that list out of every doc's markdown into ONE
  // shared array so the five sibling docs don't each carry a copy that
  // has to be kept in sync.
  //
  // Field mapping (Execution Log entry → ExecutionLogEntry):
  //   **Task 1:** …           → { id: "task-1",             status: "completed" }
  //   **Tasks 2-3:** …        → { id: "tasks-2-3",          status: "completed" }
  //   **Task 4:** …           → { id: "task-4",             status: "completed" }
  //   **Task 5:** …           → { id: "task-5",             status: "completed" }
  //   **Task 6:** …           → { id: "task-6",             status: "completed" }
  //   Skipped actions: …      → { id: "skipped-save-skill", status: "skipped"   }
  //
  // Note: the `label` values above are pre-checkmark — the ✅ emoji
  // that used to prefix "Task N" entries in the rendered body was a
  // visual encoding of `status: "completed"`. Rendering surfaces can
  // reintroduce it (or a green checkmark icon) from the structured
  // field; do NOT bake glyphs into the label strings.
  //
  // Cardinality. This array belongs to the run, not to any single
  // document — all five split docs share the same 6-entry log and
  // reach it via `sourceGroupId` / the shared metadata, NOT a per-doc
  // pointer. If a future second Auto-Learning run is added, expect
  // this to become an object keyed by run id (or move under
  // `generationMetadata.executionLog`) rather than being duplicated.
  //
  // `status` is one of "completed" | "skipped" | "warning". Not
  // consumed by any template today (same rationale as
  // `generationMetadata` above — reader surface stays quiet).
  "executionLog": [
    { "id": "task-1",             "label": "95 qualifying accounts → 31 VoiceCalls → top 10 opportunities selected", "status": "completed" },
    { "id": "tasks-2-3",          "label": "24 transcripts fetched and analyzed across 10 opportunities; 23 usable (1 no-show excluded from Tipalti)", "status": "completed" },
    { "id": "task-4",             "label": "Results stored incrementally per opportunity", "status": "completed" },
    { "id": "task-5",             "label": "5 parallel synthesis sub-passes completed (one per question)", "status": "completed" },
    { "id": "task-6",             "label": "Skill file assembled and saved to durable state (key: customer_discovery_skill_v1)", "status": "completed" },
    { "id": "skipped-save-skill", "label": "save_skill tool not available in environment; skill persisted via set_item_state only", "status": "skipped" }
  ],

  // Legacy-id → current-id redirect map, consulted by the drill-in
  // resolver in knowledge_document_detail.js so bookmarks and links
  // that still reference the pre-split single Auto-Learning document
  // land on the closest present-day equivalent (the ICP document,
  // which owns the top-level firmographic content readers most often
  // arrive looking for). The resolver reads this table only when a
  // direct `findDoc(catalog, id)` lookup misses, so unknown/non-legacy
  // ids continue to fall through to the existing "Document not
  // found" state.
  //
  // Two legacy identifiers can arrive at the drill-in resolver:
  //   1. `customer-discovery-skill-file` — the pre-split doc's `id`
  //      field, still shows up in any bookmark of the form
  //      `?id=customer-discovery-skill-file`.
  //   2. `auto-learning-customer-interactions` — the pre-split doc's
  //      URL slug, still shows up in bookmarks of the form
  //      `/knowledge/auto-learning-customer-interactions`. server.js
  //      redirects that path shape to `?id=<slug>`, so both incoming
  //      legacy shapes flow through the same client-side resolver.
  //
  // Both map to `auto-learning-icp` because ICP is the topmost content
  // in the pre-split doc's narrative (What Is Your Ideal Customer
  // Profile? — the answer readers scan for first). If a future split
  // ever gains a proper "landing / overview" doc, redirect the aliases
  // there instead. On resolve, the client uses `history.replaceState`
  // to update the URL bar to the canonical `?id=auto-learning-icp`
  // form so a re-share or reload lands directly at the current route.
  "documentAliases": {
    "customer-discovery-skill-file": "auto-learning-icp",
    "auto-learning-customer-interactions": "auto-learning-icp"
  },

  "documents": [
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Auto-Learning split (five sibling documents, one topic each).
    //
    // Previously a single "Auto-Learning from Your Past Customer
    // Interactions" record with Q1–Q5 concatenated in one markdown
    // body. Split into five per-topic documents that share:
    //   • sourceGroupId          — logical run these docs came from
    //   • generationMetadataId   — points at `generationMetadata`
    //                              (Parameter Snapshot + Execution
    //                              Log kept out of the reading
    //                              experience per the IA refactor)
    // The legacy id `customer-discovery-skill-file` is intentionally
    // dropped from `documents[]`; bookmarks land on the ICP doc via
    // the `documentAliases` map above (Step 16).
    //
    // Body markdown for each doc is stubbed here (Step 2) and filled
    // in over Steps 3–7 with the corresponding slice of the original
    // combined markdown, plus the weak-signals subsection and any
    // cross-cutting observations that belong under that topic.
    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    {
      "id": "auto-learning-icp",
      "name": "Your ICP: Who Buys From You",
      // Badged rows are down to one ("New Learnings" on Customer
      // Business Problem). Kept commented rather than deleted — see the
      // `badge` field notes at the top of this file.
      // "badge": "Auto-learned",
      "type": "Document",
      "size": "4.2 KB",
      "fileType": "txt",
      "iconSrc": "/assets/images/doctype-icons/ai.png",
      "updatedAt": "July 14",
      "sources": [
        { "name": "Salesforce", "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_salesforce.svg" },
        { "name": "Gmail", "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_gmail.png" },
        { "name": "Gong", "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_gong.svg" },
        { "name": "Calendar", "icon": "/assets/images/source_icons/source_calendar.png" }
      ],
      "updatedBy": "Issa Mao",
      "sourceGroupId": "auto-learning-customer-interactions",
      "generationMetadataId": "auto-learning-run-2026-07-28",
      "markdown": "# Ideal Customer Profile\n\n## What Is Your Ideal Customer Profile?\n\n### ICP Dimension 1: B2B SaaS / B2B Software Company\n\n**Frequency:** 9/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** High\n\nEvery opportunity in the dataset is a B2B software company. This is the foundational firmographic qualifier.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. Mixpanel: Enterprise B2B SaaS with dedicated demand generation team and multi-region SDR coverage\n2. TravelPerk: Mid-market SaaS with BDR+SE team structure, 45-day sales cycle\n3. Udemy: B2B SaaS with global BDR teams, ~$25K ACV, 40 seats across engagement tools\n4. Zone & Co: FinTech B2B company transitioning from inbound to outbound\n\n### ICP Dimension 2: Sizeable SDR/BDR Team (15+ Reps)\n\n**Frequency:** 7/9 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Branch, Diligent, Udemy, Optimizely, Movable Ink) | **Confidence:** High\n\nStrong signal: 7 of 9 opportunities have 15+ SDRs/BDRs. The product's value scales with team size.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. Diligent: 50-100+ BDRs across acquisitions\n2. Optimizely: 47 SDRs deployed globally\n3. Movable Ink: 25-30 SDRs, outbound-heavy\n4. Branch: 15+ BDRs, VC-backed mid-market SaaS\n\n### ICP Dimension 3: Outbound-Oriented Sales Motion\n\n**Frequency:** 5/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** High\n\nOutbound-heavy or actively transitioning to outbound. The product's value proposition centers on automating outbound workflows.\n\n### ICP Dimension 4: Existing Intent/ABM Tool Investment (6Sense, Demandbase, UserGems)\n\n**Frequency:** 5/9 opportunities (Workato, Udemy, Optimizely, Zone & Co, Branch) | **Confidence:** High\n\nCustomers already invested in intent/ABM tools and looking to complement, consolidate, or replace them.\n\n### ICP Dimension 5: Uses Conversation Intelligence (Gong)\n\n**Frequency:** 5/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n### ICP Dimension 6: Salesforce as Primary CRM\n\n**Frequency:** 5/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n### ICP Dimension 7: Multi-Tool Sales Tech Stack (4+ Tools)\n\n**Frequency:** 5/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** High\n\nCustomers using 4+ GTM tools (ZoomInfo, Gong, Demandbase, 6Sense, Outreach, Nooks, etc.) — creating both the pain (tool sprawl) and the opportunity (consolidation).\n\n### ICP Dimension 8: Global / Multi-Region Sales Teams\n\n**Frequency:** 4/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n### ICP Dimension 9: High Call Volume / Activity-Dense Pipeline\n\n**Frequency:** 4/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n### ICP Dimension 10: Uses Sales Engagement Platform (Outreach/SalesLoft/Nooks)\n\n**Frequency:** 4/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n### ICP Dimension 11: Uses ZoomInfo for Data Enrichment\n\n**Frequency:** 3/9 opportunities | **Confidence:** Medium\n\n## Emerging and Weak Signals\n\n- **AI Agent / Automated Messaging Quality** (3 transcripts, 1 opp — Mixpanel only): AI agent mixing up persona messaging, QA bottlenecks. Single-opp signal.\n- **Internal Organizational Blockers** (2 transcripts, 1 opp — Diligent only): Internal politics and failed prior implementations blocking tool adoption.\n\n## Key Takeaway\n\n**ICP sweet spot:** B2B SaaS with 15+ BDRs, Salesforce-based, already invested in 4+ GTM tools, outbound-oriented or transitioning to outbound. These companies have both the pain (manual prospecting, tool sprawl) and the infrastructure (CRM, SEP) to integrate immediately.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-learning-business-problem",
